# Two findings in a single commit, both false positives, both now fixed at the
# source so no new occurrence can be created. They are pinned here by exact
# fingerprint (commit:file:rule:line) rather than allowlisted by regex or by
# path, because a fingerprint cannot suppress anything except these two
# historical lines. A regex or path allowlist would also cover every future
# finding of the same shape in the same files, which is the hole this file
# exists to avoid.
#
# What they were: V2-091 built its session-token test fixtures as a prefix
# constant plus a suffix constant, following the instruction to concatenate so
# that no secret-shaped literal appears. That instruction was not sufficient.
# The suffix half was still 16 hex digits, and the identifier holding it
# contained the substring "Token", which is one of generic-api-key's trigger
# keywords -- so the line matched on the keyword plus the high-entropy quoted
# value even though the whole token was never written down.
#
# The fix at source: the high-entropy part is now COMPUTED with
# strings.Repeat over a four-character group, so no quoted value in either
# file has the shape of a credential. Neither fixture ever was a credential:
# both are local test doubles for a runner session token and neither was ever
# accepted by anything but a stub.
#
# The rule itself is untouched. Recorded in docs/operations/v2-task-dag.md
# section 9.7.
